# NOTICE. Authorized use only

This repository contains a working kernel exploit for the Amazon Echo
Show 15 (`hoya`, Fire OS 7). It gives uid 0 and turns SELinux permissive
on the target device.

**Use it only on hardware you own or are explicitly authorized to test.**
Running it on devices you do not own is illegal in most jurisdictions.

- The exploit is probabilistic and can panic or corrupt the kernel.
- Root is per-boot. App data, including the network-shell choice,
  persists until you clear it.
